Written and verified. `ADR-001-notification-architecture.md` is in the workdir — **EXCELLENT** against the research challenge validator, all 9 checks passing (canonical sections in order, single definitive commitment, pros/cons in Consequences, rejected option in Alternatives, 12/12 technical properties, 1870 words).

**Recommendation: Redis Streams.** Decision rests on four points: (1) at 10x the workload is ~10³ msg/s, two orders of magnitude below a single Redis node's 100k+ ops/s, so Kafka's millions-of-msg/s throughput is irrelevant; (2) Kafka's exactly-once (KIP-98) is scoped to the broker and cannot make webhook/email delivery exactly-once anyway — the outbox + idempotent-consumer pattern is required on either broker, so Kafka's flagship feature buys nothing; (3) the 6-person team with no infra engineer and no Kafka experience, plus the 2-week constraint and no Confluent budget, makes self-hosted Kafka a permanent ops tax; (4) Redis is already in production, so Streams adds zero new infrastructure and doubles as the fan-out hub for the WebSocket gateway. Kafka's genuine advantages — time-based retention, replay, ecosystem — are nice-to-haves the outbox makes unnecessary; the broker-agnostic outbox keeps a Kafka migration affordable if the platform ever becomes an event bus.
